  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The recurrence returns to the DQ-CTM thought stage, while the dense carrier continues through the end-to-end image flow.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes a dense feature field, then it is partitioned into windows without leaving the spatial carrier. The compact thought process reads and updates that carrier over repeated ticks. The recurrence returns to the thought stage itself, and the same parameters are used across ticks. The decoder turns the updated dense carrier back into the super-resolved output.",
      "evidence": [
