      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation separates dense feature construction from window partitioning, while keeping the tokens tied to the carrier.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The first term says the encoder turns the low-resolution image into a dense feature field. The second term partitions that field into windows. The window tokens come from the dense field, so the carrier is kept instead of discarded.",
